    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "Across the spectrum German outlets uniformly highlight the scale of job cuts in the automotive industry, especially Porsche, as a central driver of labour-market insecurity. They also converge on the diagnosis that a persistent skills shortage, intensified by digitalisation and automation, demands a coordinated expansion of vocational training and reskilling programmes. Finally, there is a shared concern that rising social-security outlays and the cost impact of the minimum-wage policy strain fiscal sustainability, prompting calls for structural reforms of pensions and basic-income schemes.",
